00:19:25.345 --> 00:19:29.433
using, assessing.
Often students who are really smart and

e48cae51-35de-49ce-b9f3-3dd3c48cd19d-7
00:19:29.433 --> 00:19:30.350
really driven

4d1a3422-6953-4124-a2ac-ea77807059a6-0
00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:35.590
skip over learning vocabulary and
learning objectives like define or state

67670b15-1b63-4add-86c2-4f584bae546e-0
00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:40.300
almost all of the verbs that are on
understand because it feels superficial.

67670b15-1b63-4add-86c2-4f584bae546e-1
00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.520
They want to get right to the application,

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-0
00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:48.424
and oftentimes people do this because
learning definitions feels kind of

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-1
00:19:48.424 --> 00:19:51.597
remedial.
But learning vocabulary does not mean

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-2
00:19:51.597 --> 00:19:55.562
engaging with complexity.
When we think about the nature of

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-3
00:19:55.562 --> 00:19:58.801
complexity,
you need to understand the component

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-4
00:19:58.801 --> 00:20:01.643
parts,
because there are a lot of discrete

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-5
00:20:01.643 --> 00:20:04.816
pieces,
and in order to engage with all of them

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-6
00:20:04.816 --> 00:20:08.054
together,
you need to be able to understand them

6209d370-21de-48f4-aad1-e499a5b8b7d5-7
00:20:08.054 --> 00:20:08.979
fundamentally.

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-0
00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:14.264
Oftentimes,
students think that good learning means

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-1
00:20:14.264 --> 00:20:17.535
learning the material 1st and then
testing their knowledge.

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-2
00:20:17.535 --> 00:20:21.732
So a lot of students save practice
problems for what they feel for what they

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-3
00:20:21.732 --> 00:20:24.512
feel like they've actually learned
something. Now,

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-4
00:20:24.512 --> 00:20:27.946
that's not a bad way of doing things,
and there's logic to it,

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-5
00:20:27.946 --> 00:20:32.089
but it can be really hard to start this
way when learning complex material,

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-6
00:20:32.089 --> 00:20:36.613
especially when the stakes feel high and
you have a lot of other material to study

6ba0138b-9c27-4b52-bcab-be8272cd2831-7
00:20:36.613 --> 00:20:37.540
in other courses.

2d1e4fd5-5846-4956-9f1e-105f085bf276-0
00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:42.074
So an approach that we recommend is
instead to invert the logic.

2d1e4fd5-5846-4956-9f1e-105f085bf276-1
00:20:42.074 --> 00:20:46.690
Rather than thinking about learning the
material and then applying your knowledge,

2d1e4fd5-5846-4956-9f1e-105f085bf276-2
00:20:46.690 --> 00:20:51.249
try thinking about applying the questions
to the material as you are learning it.

5c97bf0d-fb6e-4e82-8019-651d3dadd975-0
00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:56.779
Use the questions and practice problems
as tools for organizing your

5c97bf0d-fb6e-4e82-8019-651d3dadd975-1
00:20:56.779 --> 00:21:02.208
understanding of the material and as you
build up your ability to make use of the

5c97bf0d-fb6e-4e82-8019-651d3dadd975-2
00:21:02.208 --> 00:21:06.579
details that you're learning.
The purpose of doing this is to use

5c97bf0d-fb6e-4e82-8019-651d3dadd975-3
00:21:06.579 --> 00:21:10.883
questions as a guide to exploring
concepts, and as you practice,

5c97bf0d-fb6e-4e82-8019-651d3dadd975-4
00:21:10.883 --> 00:21:15.584
applying the concepts to solving problems
and thinking things through.

5c97bf0d-fb6e-4e82-8019-651d3dadd975-5
00:21:15.584 --> 00:21:21.213
So as you're thinking about each question,
rather than initially trying to answer it

5c97bf0d-fb6e-4e82-8019-651d3dadd975-6
00:21:21.213 --> 00:21:22.670
or solve it, try first

660ede3a-6461-4950-84f1-05bf07c795ae-0
00:21:22.850 --> 00:21:27.898
identify the components in that question
that you need to know and then the things

660ede3a-6461-4950-84f1-05bf07c795ae-1
00:21:27.898 --> 00:21:30.270
that that question is asking you to do.

18cb197b-fd7a-45d9-b761-754951420b22-0
00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:35.462
Through your practice,
you will encounter problems that are

18cb197b-fd7a-45d9-b761-754951420b22-1
00:21:35.462 --> 00:21:39.907
easily solvable and ones that are more
challenging for the challenging and novel.

18cb197b-fd7a-45d9-b761-754951420b22-2
00:21:39.907 --> 00:21:44.244
Once we encourage students to think very
deliberately about the problem solving

18cb197b-fd7a-45d9-b761-754951420b22-3
00:21:44.244 --> 00:21:44.570
steps,

5927d0f6-5c66-4eb8-8e81-de4d4b62cda7-0
00:21:45.890 --> 00:21:52.282
step one is understanding the question.
Read the question carefully and write the

5927d0f6-5c66-4eb8-8e81-de4d4b62cda7-1
00:21:52.282 --> 00:21:58.129
data that you are provided in short form.
Identify variables, terminology,

5927d0f6-5c66-4eb8-8e81-de4d4b62cda7-2
00:21:58.129 --> 00:22:03.118
and thinking actions.
What kinds of thinking are being asked of

5927d0f6-5c66-4eb8-8e81-de4d4b62cda7-3
00:22:03.118 --> 00:22:03.430
you?

c77065c7-33ef-46e5-b188-d9d32a3bc73a-0
00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:08.510
Are you being asked to recognize, analyze,
compare?

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-0
00:22:09.610 --> 00:22:14.635
Then you want to review any graphical or
visual information that's also being

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-1
00:22:14.635 --> 00:22:17.792
provided,
and then you want to attempt to answer

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-2
00:22:17.792 --> 00:22:23.075
that question. What are the components?
Every concept it touches lists those out.

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-3
00:22:23.075 --> 00:22:26.361
What theory or rules are you being asked
to apply?

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-4
00:22:26.361 --> 00:22:29.969
Can you state the relationships between
these concepts?

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-5
00:22:29.969 --> 00:22:33.255
And what are you being asked to do with
all of it?

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-6
00:22:33.255 --> 00:22:37.249
Write these answers down rather than
doing this in your head,

bd2ad24e-6b78-4f91-9eec-4809ce84bc9d-7
00:22:37.249 --> 00:22:40.020
because what this allows you to do is
make

9c4ab416-cf4b-468c-a3a7-f76d3c6db120-0
00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:41.750
construction vision visible

14cfaaa1-3eb2-45b9-995d-d47ea5b2670c-0
00:22:42.420 --> 00:22:46.364
and make.
Writing that list on paper is a way to

14cfaaa1-3eb2-45b9-995d-d47ea5b2670c-1
00:22:46.364 --> 00:22:50.229
get at what feels good and where your
gaps are.

14cfaaa1-3eb2-45b9-995d-d47ea5b2670c-2
00:22:50.229 --> 00:22:54.093
This frequently unsticks the problem by
itself,

14cfaaa1-3eb2-45b9-995d-d47ea5b2670c-3
00:22:54.093 --> 00:23:00.533
and a question that looked impenetrable
often turns out to be 3 things you know

14cfaaa1-3eb2-45b9-995d-d47ea5b2670c-4
00:23:00.533 --> 00:23:03.110
arranged in an unfamiliar order.

1e03a79f-a87a-405e-890b-fa1af4fa0e92-0
00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:07.623
Also,
when you are thinking about places where

1e03a79f-a87a-405e-890b-fa1af4fa0e92-1
00:23:07.623 --> 00:23:11.385
you're stuck,
that's a point when to engage AI.

1e03a79f-a87a-405e-890b-fa1af4fa0e92-2
00:23:11.385 --> 00:23:17.498
Not just asking the entire question,
but thinking about exactly where you are

1e03a79f-a87a-405e-890b-fa1af4fa0e92-3
00:23:17.498 --> 00:23:21.260
and that component that you're concerned
about.

41298746-077b-4d42-929a-3eca91f11fe0-0
00:23:23.730 --> 00:23:28.130
So if you get stuck,
do you have enough information and data

41298746-077b-4d42-929a-3eca91f11fe0-1
00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:32.891
to answer the question?
Have you understood the question clearly?

41298746-077b-4d42-929a-3eca91f11fe0-2
00:23:32.891 --> 00:23:38.374
Reflect on what rules or equations or
theories or approaches you learned in

41298746-077b-4d42-929a-3eca91f11fe0-3
00:23:38.374 --> 00:23:41.548
class that might apply here.
List them off.

41298746-077b-4d42-929a-3eca91f11fe0-4
00:23:41.548 --> 00:23:47.103
Can you break the problem into steps?
Those that you know and those that are

41298746-077b-4d42-929a-3eca91f11fe0-5
00:23:47.103 --> 00:23:51.503
unclear, Hint, hint.
That unclear part is where you're going

41298746-077b-4d42-929a-3eca91f11fe0-6
00:23:51.503 --> 00:23:53.740
to go back to your material, or

3a8695cf-72bd-47b9-98ae-efff074ace1a-0
00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:58.050
ask a Prof, a TA, a tutor,
or engage with AI

584423f5-f411-4bfc-81c6-784d74fb064b-0
00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:05.380
and then think about what within your
coursework so far resembles this problem.

4bf415b9-c82b-42e4-a5dc-caa3e5118095-0
00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:12.110
Now this is the part

7b7d606a-5a38-405c-8d34-98108c25506a-0
00:24:12.940 --> 00:24:16.366
that decides whether step three helps or
hurts.

7b7d606a-5a38-405c-8d34-98108c25506a-1
00:24:16.366 --> 00:24:21.076
Reading through a worked solution is
nearly worthless, and worse,

7b7d606a-5a38-405c-8d34-98108c25506a-2
00:24:21.076 --> 00:24:25.216
it feels productive,
and it makes sense as you go and you

7b7d606a-5a38-405c-8d34-98108c25506a-3
00:24:25.216 --> 00:24:30.569
finish believing you could do it.
But it actually doesn't mean that you've

7b7d606a-5a38-405c-8d34-98108c25506a-4
00:24:30.569 --> 00:24:33.996
learned it.
You want to be able to work it out,

7b7d606a-5a38-405c-8d34-98108c25506a-5
00:24:33.996 --> 00:24:38.350
writing out every step in your own hand
as you follow along.

daacf080-2d49-4177-be4f-3395e0a95dd9-0
00:24:40.880 --> 00:24:46.805
Now at each step you're going to stop and
ask the question, why am I doing this?

daacf080-2d49-4177-be4f-3395e0a95dd9-1
00:24:46.805 --> 00:24:51.194
What is this step for,
and how does it fit into solving the

daacf080-2d49-4177-be4f-3395e0a95dd9-2
00:24:51.194 --> 00:24:51.780
problem?

44cd4d05-5f87-469f-bd0d-eb7609d4b060-0
00:24:53.070 --> 00:24:57.606
If you cannot answer,
you have found the exact point where you

44cd4d05-5f87-469f-bd0d-eb7609d4b060-1
00:24:57.606 --> 00:25:02.070
are copying rather than understanding.
Then close the sample,

44cd4d05-5f87-469f-bd0d-eb7609d4b060-2
00:25:02.070 --> 00:25:07.039
go back to your own problem,
and apply what you've learned about the

44cd4d05-5f87-469f-bd0d-eb7609d4b060-3
00:25:07.039 --> 00:25:10.423
approach rather than reproducing what you
saw.

44cd4d05-5f87-469f-bd0d-eb7609d4b060-4
00:25:10.423 --> 00:25:16.040
This is the difference between having a
method and having memorized a method.

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-0
00:25:16.920 --> 00:25:19.922
So when you think about reflect and
review,

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-1
00:25:19.922 --> 00:25:23.060
it's not just about getting the right
answer.

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-2
00:25:23.060 --> 00:25:27.290
You want to reflect on what you know and
what you don't know,

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-3
00:25:27.290 --> 00:25:31.384
and that's what's going to help you ace
future assessments.

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-4
00:25:31.384 --> 00:25:34.795
Are there patterns in problem solving
challenges?

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-5
00:25:34.795 --> 00:25:40.117
Is there a concept that you are unclear
on and that you need more support on?

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-6
00:25:40.117 --> 00:25:43.255
This is when you can start using other
tools,

17a83828-232c-43dc-b38e-0d69bf253822-7
00:25:43.255 --> 00:25:46.939
but you really want to do is get into
these component

0a63a376-1ec6-4d59-bac9-967f1b4bdf57-0
00:25:47.010 --> 00:25:50.810
problems before asking AI for support.

ce1cfbdb-7adb-4526-a6cc-126a90892d45-0
00:25:52.750 --> 00:25:56.529
And are there any traps that you need to
watch out for?

ce1cfbdb-7adb-4526-a6cc-126a90892d45-1
00:25:56.529 --> 00:26:01.456
Do you make the same mistake over and
over again and can you explain the

ce1cfbdb-7adb-4526-a6cc-126a90892d45-2
00:26:01.456 --> 00:26:04.493
problem and translate the problem to a
peer?

ce1cfbdb-7adb-4526-a6cc-126a90892d45-3
00:26:04.493 --> 00:26:09.892
One thing to take from these three steps
is that they are layered deliberately.

ce1cfbdb-7adb-4526-a6cc-126a90892d45-4
00:26:09.892 --> 00:26:14.953
This order is going to really work.
Going straight to work solution when a

ce1cfbdb-7adb-4526-a6cc-126a90892d45-5
00:26:14.953 --> 00:26:20.487
problem was actually a concept gap wastes
the sample problem and teaches nothing.

ce1cfbdb-7adb-4526-a6cc-126a90892d45-6
00:26:20.487 --> 00:26:23.120
And this is where AI can get in the way

9da0a9c0-948a-4078-aff3-4f69aa067412-0
00:26:23.220 --> 00:26:26.010
of getting to the good meat of learning.

7ef75b92-ff36-4b99-966c-e36b23b83f74-0
00:26:26.990 --> 00:26:32.315
Rereading the chapter where you had a
skill gap also waste time and sometimes

7ef75b92-ff36-4b99-966c-e36b23b83f74-1
00:26:32.315 --> 00:26:36.617
waste a lot of time.
So you need to follow each of these steps

7ef75b92-ff36-4b99-966c-e36b23b83f74-2
00:26:36.617 --> 00:26:40.100
to figure out exactly where the pain
point gap is.

216fb808-c63c-4172-9652-2a9f658b9e71-0
00:26:42.240 --> 00:26:46.811
Remember that discussion about
understanding and applying and moving

216fb808-c63c-4172-9652-2a9f658b9e71-1
00:26:46.811 --> 00:26:50.587
between the two? Well,
if you haven't seen this already,

216fb808-c63c-4172-9652-2a9f658b9e71-2
00:26:50.587 --> 00:26:54.828
this is Blooms Taxonomy.
This is the way we understand material

216fb808-c63c-4172-9652-2a9f658b9e71-3
00:26:54.828 --> 00:26:59.399
from the very foundational just
remembering to the ability to create

216fb808-c63c-4172-9652-2a9f658b9e71-4
00:26:59.399 --> 00:27:04.235
something new out of the material.
But this isn't a one way process from

216fb808-c63c-4172-9652-2a9f658b9e71-5
00:27:04.235 --> 00:27:08.409
remembering to creating. In fact,
as we are learning material,

216fb808-c63c-4172-9652-2a9f658b9e71-6
00:27:08.409 --> 00:27:12.650
we need to loop back through different
levels of understanding,

383fbc34-3b8b-4d85-bfb9-c67a714cfd41-0
00:27:12.730 --> 00:27:16.896
go back to definitions,
try to remember what those definitions

383fbc34-3b8b-4d85-bfb9-c67a714cfd41-1
00:27:16.896 --> 00:27:19.938
mean,
challenging ourselves to understand it,

383fbc34-3b8b-4d85-bfb9-c67a714cfd41-2
00:27:19.938 --> 00:27:23.378
go back and apply,
analyze what components we don't

383fbc34-3b8b-4d85-bfb9-c67a714cfd41-3
00:27:23.378 --> 00:27:26.751
understand,
and go back and remember and challenge

383fbc34-3b8b-4d85-bfb9-c67a714cfd41-4
00:27:26.751 --> 00:27:28.140
those concepts again.

510ef095-a095-4d4d-b088-f297c27afbd1-0
00:27:28.870 --> 00:27:33.776
So it really is an iterative process and
one that you're going to want to engage

510ef095-a095-4d4d-b088-f297c27afbd1-1
00:27:33.776 --> 00:27:36.320
with as you work on those sample problems.

dea8b0c5-ab2e-47f8-8dc0-c54183e57dc6-0
00:27:37.610 --> 00:27:40.868
Now,
in a complex problem solving course like

dea8b0c5-ab2e-47f8-8dc0-c54183e57dc6-1
00:27:40.868 --> 00:27:44.552
Stats 237,
a common trap that students fall into is

dea8b0c5-ab2e-47f8-8dc0-c54183e57dc6-2
00:27:44.552 --> 00:27:48.307
plug and chug,
where they're taking information from

dea8b0c5-ab2e-47f8-8dc0-c54183e57dc6-3
00:27:48.307 --> 00:27:54.045
slides or the board without a structure.
They ask their friends or AI to solve a

dea8b0c5-ab2e-47f8-8dc0-c54183e57dc6-4
00:27:54.045 --> 00:27:59.499
problem for them and they just remember
the steps and memorize the solution.

dea8b0c5-ab2e-47f8-8dc0-c54183e57dc6-5
00:27:59.499 --> 00:28:03.962
We don't want to do that.
And that's a real danger of using AI

dea8b0c5-ab2e-47f8-8dc0-c54183e57dc6-6
00:28:03.962 --> 00:28:07.930
where it might look like it gives you
steps to applying

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-0
00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:11.096
no problem.
But when those problems get much more

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-1
00:28:11.096 --> 00:28:15.616
complex, the steps fall apart.
And so you can miss the main point of how

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-2
00:28:15.616 --> 00:28:18.713
formulas and concepts connect and can be
applied.

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-3
00:28:18.713 --> 00:28:23.048
And you have this illusion of
understanding that you can follow along

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-4
00:28:23.048 --> 00:28:28.126
because you recognize what's being done,
but you're just kind of plugging numbers

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-5
00:28:28.126 --> 00:28:33.265
into somebody else's decision making and
thinking rather than the ability to do it

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-6
00:28:33.265 --> 00:28:36.362
yourself.
So it can be very easy to miss the main

04d16d68-ba7c-4274-9e7c-9b8ac8b34f29-7
00:28:36.362 --> 00:28:38.220
point of some of these pieces,

